>I was playing nethack tonight and got a crazy idea.  I was in a temple
>and had a ring of polymorph and a ring of polymorph control and 400 times
>my level in gold.  I polymorphed myself into a leprechaun and
>preceeded to gift and steal the gold from the priestess.  I ended up with
>an armor class of -98 without armor and rings when I returned to human
>form!  With armor I'm AC -124 but it loops around to 127 or so when I
>put on the ring of protection (+5!) that I found.  I am not
>disappointed with this.  Mainly, I am curious why the priestess does
>not get angry and attack me as a leprechaun, but does when I polymorph
>into a nymph and try to steal her stuff.  Has anyone else done this?

This is not anything new (that I know of).  Another one of my favorite methods
is to make a large area filled with tamed leprechauns and random items.  Each
time one of your little pets drops something they have picked up, they drop
money behind too.  Works with Orcs too.

Anyway, the reason she/he does not attack you is that he/she has not been hit
by you.  If you steal money, you are not attacking.  Now, if you are  
trying to steal and you fail, THEN you will attack them (on the same move)
so WATCH OUT.

